# Task FEATURE-003-US-002-T01 — Implement: Score model & data contracts

> **DaemonCore coding-agent prompt.** Work type: `feature` · Size: `S` · Priority: `P1` · Status: `todo`

## Where this fits
- **Epic EPIC-003 — Deterministic Scoring Engine.** Generate transparent, explainable, deterministic scores across eight policy outcome categories, with a configurable weighting system and per-score rationale. No AI anywhere in the scoring path.
- **Feature FEATURE-003 — Deterministic Scoring Engine — implementation.**
- **Story FEATURE-003-US-002 — Score model & data contracts.** _As a developer, I want typed score objects so categories are consistent._

## Objective
As a developer, I want typed score objects so categories are consistent.

## What to do
Implement the capability so that every acceptance criterion below holds. Specifically:
- ScoreResult carries per-category value, weight and rationale
- The 0-100 scale is enforced in the type
- Score objects are serialisable for storage with a model
Add or update docstrings and any necessary types. Keep the change focused on this story; do not pull in scope from other stories/epics.

## Acceptance criteria (Definition of Done)
- [ ] ScoreResult carries per-category value, weight and rationale
- [ ] The 0-100 scale is enforced in the type
- [ ] Score objects are serialisable for storage with a model
- [ ] New/updated tests pass and cover the above
- [ ] No regression in the existing `pytest` suite

## Dependencies
None within this story. (Respect cross-epic dependencies of the parent epic.)

## Project conventions
- Target Python 3.13. Use British spelling in all user-facing text.
- Keep the pure model layer (`model/`) free of Streamlit; `app.py` is UI/render only.
- Pin any new runtime deps in `requirements.txt`; test-only deps in `requirements-dev.txt`.
- Write deterministic `pytest` tests; follow the style of `tests/test_fiscal_model.py`.
- Match the surrounding code style. Prefer small, coherent diffs over broad refactors.
- Update `README.md` / `docs/` whenever behaviour changes.

## Guardrails (EPIC-003)
- Scoring MUST be deterministic — NO AI and no randomness in the scoring path.
- Every score must carry a plain-English rationale.
- Weightings must be externally configurable and documented.
- Normalise scores to the documented common scale (e.g. 0–100).

